ic nominee a clear favorite, and with no polls, ratings, or candidate-level financial data available, the forecast rests on the state's fundamentals. The absence of any evidence of a competitive Republican operation keeps the race in Likely D rather than Tossup territory.", "watch": "Any published Hawaii polling showing a much narrower margin, or a sharply nationalized environment breaking against Democrats, would be the main reason to revisit this rating.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No expert ratings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Hawaii remains one of the most Democratic-leaning states in presidential elections, with a partisan lean of roughly thirteen points favoring Democrats. The incumbent president is term-limited, so neither side benefits from incumbency, and no candidate-specific fundraising or outside spending figures are available for the generic nominees. No public polls of the state or expert race ratings have been published, so the outlook rests on the state's underlying partisan fundamentals.\n\nWith a thirteen-point expected margin and uncertainty of about nine points, the Democratic nominee is a clear favorite, though not at the level of a safe rating. Hawaii's presidential results have been consistently lopsided in recent cycles, and there is little sign of a competitive Republican operation in the state. The main source of uncertainty is the absence of polling rather than any evidence of a genuine contest.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9253, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8734, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8703, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9295, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.874, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.8784, "margin":